<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Freiberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Freiberg is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ore-mountains">Ore Mountains</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">Silver</a> was discovered there around 1168, setting off a mining rush that made the margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> rich and the town one of the largest in the region. Its mining academy, the Bergakademie, founded in 1765, is the oldest university of mining and metallurgy in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/freiberg.jpg" alt="Freiberg" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Kolossos · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Freiberg-Petri-Obermarkt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
